.\" -*- mode: troff; coding: utf-8 -*-
.TH UPDATECONF 8
.SH NAME
updateconf \- merge .new configuration files after package upgrades
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
After a package upgrade, \fBspm\fR(8) leaves updated stock
configuration files next to the live ones with a \fI.new\fR suffix.
\fBupdateconf\fR walks the configuration directory, shows a unified
diff for every \fI*.new\fR file, and interactively asks what to do with
it:
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
U|update: replace the live file with the .new version
D|discard: remove the .new file
E|edit: open the live file in $EDITOR and ask again
K|keep: leave both files in place
.TE
.LP
A \fI.new\fR file whose live counterpart no longer exists is removed
automatically; a \fI.new\fR file with no differences is removed without
asking.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fI<dir>\fR
Directory to scan (default \fI/etc\fR).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBEDITOR\fR
Editor used for the \fIedit\fR action (default \fIvi\fR).
.TP
\fBAMU_ROOT\fR
When set to a directory other than \fI/\fR, the scan root is taken
relative to it.

.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/etc\fR
Default scan directory.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amu (8),
.BR diff (1)

